ue of $k$?" 13194139536001 17592186045417 false] [17592186192407 1071 "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{kx + 6}{x-4}, \\qquad x\\neq 4\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{4x+6}{x-2}, \\qquad x\\neq 2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192407 1074 "To find $f^{-1}(x)$, we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{kx + 6}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{ky+6}{y-4}\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= \\frac{ky + 6}{y - 4} \\\\\nx(y - 4) &= ky + 6 \\\\\nxy - 4x &= ky + 6 \\\\\nxy - ky &= 4x + 6 \\\\\ny(x - k) &= 4x + 6 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4x + 6}{x - k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{4x+6}{x-k}\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=2$." 13194139536001 17592186045417 false] [17592186192407 1074 "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny =  \\dfrac{kx + 6}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{ky+6}{y-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{ky+6}{y-4} \\\\ x(y-4) & =ky+6 \\\\ xy-4x & =ky+6 \\\\ xy-ky & =4x+6 \\\\ y(x-k) & =4x+6 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+6}{x-k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{4x+6}{x-k}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=2.$" 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192634 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555821 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555766 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555808 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192698 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555781 13194139536001 17592186045417 true] [17592186192699 1038 #edb/ref 17592186555760 13194139536001 17592186045417 tr